      {
        "reagents": [
          "#alkyl_halide_1"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": {
      "summary": "Alkoxide + CH₃ or 1° halide → ether (SN2). The alkoxide can be anything; the halide must be CH₃ or 1° (benzyl and allyl are great).",
      "notes": [
        "Order matters: base first, then the halide.",
        "A 2°/3° halide gives E2 instead (see E4)."
